[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [[:db/retract 17592186121850 :answer-field/choices 17592186121851] [:db/retract 17592186121850 :answer-field/choices 17592186121852] [:db/retract 17592186121850 :answer-field/choices 17592186121853] [:db/retract 17592186121850 :answer-field/choices 17592186121854] [:db/retract 17592186121850 :answer-field/choices 17592186121855] {:db/id 17592186124583 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-df827c7e-ce3b-5b89-941a-437f86328b7a" "question-25370e2a-dfa1-5d6f-b02b-964c5925c1f3"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124391 :question/problem "What is the domain of the function $g(x)=\\dfrac{4}{3}x^2+5x -12?$" :question/worked-solution "A quadratic function is defined for all real numbers.\n\nTherefore, the domain of $g(x)$ is $x\\in(-\\infty,\\infty).$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124584 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-0bc8d353-4f35-531e-9326-d4dcbc01bbdb" "question-9acd8689-6770-5d1b-9670-f2ff78d7e31a"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124393 :question/problem "What is the range of the function $f(x) = (x+3)^2-2?$" :question/worked-solution "The parabola is written in vertex form, \n\n$$\ny = a(x-h)^2 + k,\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ is the leading coefficient and $(h,k)$ is the vertex. \n\n- Since $h=-3$ and $k=-2,$ the vertex is $(-3,-2).$\n\n- Since $a=1>0,$ the parabola opens upwards.\n\nBecause the parabola opens upwards, the vertex corresponds to the minimum output, while there is no maximum output. \n\nTherefore, the range is $[-2,\\infty).$\n\nThe corresponding diagram is shown below.\n\n![](images/57/579eef7814c2b51c44cded6fb2dc64e36d1106d359864e1e7ec7354511f80681.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124659 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-c749b226-6df0-583d-9d39-da82636ab3b6" "question-0eda0ab3-fc3e-57ae-8050-823c01afb804" "question-7dfd6f87-7029-50ed-aece-aeae8cb98e8c" "question-28ef6032-c464-5039-b5ee-d8d9a6314099"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124225 :question/problem "What is the range of the function $f(x)=x^2+4x+6?$" :question/worked-solution "The given parabola is written in standard form,\n\n$$\ny = ax^2+bx+c,\n$$\n\nwith $a=1>0,$ $b=4,$ and $c=6.$\n\nBecause the leading coefficient is positive, the parabola opens upward. Consequently, there is no maximum output, and the vertex corresponds to the minimum output.\n\nThe $x$-coordinate of the vertex is given by\n\n$$\nx= -\\dfrac{b}{2a} = -\\dfrac{4}{2 \\cdot 1} = -2.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $x=-2$ back into the function to find the $y$-value of the vertex:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={x}^{2}+4x+6 \\\\  & =(-2)^{2}+4(-2)+6 \\\\  & =4-8+6 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vertex is $(-2,2),$ and the range of the function is $[2,\\infty).$\n\n![](images/41/41b7219793120c0e37b3d910ef6a8f3754c1d9f27b784f937381743d7b7a85df.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124660 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-0dff1477-477e-5350-b60a-a888d8f2c5e5"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124226 :question/problem "What is the range of the function $f(x) = -\\dfrac{1}{2}(x+3)(x-1)?$" :question/worked-solution "The given parabola is written in factored form,\n\n$$\ny = a(x-x_1)(x-x_2),\n$$\n\nwith $a = -\\dfrac{1}{2} <    0.$ \n\nBecause the leading coefficient is negative, the parabola opens downward. Consequently, there is no minimum output, and the vertex corresponds to the maximum output.\n\nThe two roots of the parabola are $x_1=-3$ and $x_2=1,$ and we can find the $x$-coordinate of the vertex by taking the average of the roots:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2}=\\frac{-3+1}{2}=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $x=-1$ back into the function to find the $y$-value of the vertex:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-\\frac{1}{2}(x+3)(x-1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}(-1+3)(-1-1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vertex is $(-1,2),$ and the range of the function is $(-\\infty,2].$\n\n![](images/2f/2f949680675dd0b0347adc154b8be6ce301ddb2f5b1b9ab0c077a5c00f81568f.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-df827c7e-ce3b-5b89-941a-437f86328b7a" :question/id #uuid "df827c7e-ce3b-5b89-941a-437f86328b7a" :question/math-academy-id "q-106274" :question/problem "What is the domain of the function $h(x)=8{x}^{2}-4x-1?$" :question/worked-solution "A quadratic function is defined for all real numbers.\n\nTherefore, the domain of $h(x)$ is $x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-829f5ab0-8ba8-548c-bb23-b5d76fbb4d22"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-829f5ab0-8ba8-548c-bb23-b5d76fbb4d22" :answer-field/id #uuid "829f5ab0-8ba8-548c-bb23-b5d76fbb4d22" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-db13116f-35b5-5cb0-bb88-3f745d6dbe2f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-db13116f-35b5-5cb0-bb88-3f745d6dbe2f" "answer-902ebbab-7478-5af7-9256-7c8f862f93a6" "answer-44c76b2d-2338-5b08-8808-f24cc8ea5181" "answer-99fd63fa-18e6-55ea-901a-0243576aa56a" "answer-537557a3-a7a3-54ed-be9a-305c2144a33d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-db13116f-35b5-5cb0-bb88-3f745d6dbe2f" :answer/id #uuid "db13116f-35b5-5cb0-bb88-3f745d6dbe2f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-902ebbab-7478-5af7-9256-7c8f862f93a6" :answer/id #uuid "902ebbab-7478-5af7-9256-7c8f862f93a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\in [-1,4]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-44c76b2d-2338-5b08-8808-f24cc8ea5181" :answer/id #uuid "44c76b2d-2338-5b08-8808-f24cc8ea5181" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\in [-4,8]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-99fd63fa-18e6-55ea-901a-0243576aa56a" :answer/id #uuid "99fd63fa-18e6-55ea-901a-0243576aa5